reuse-coretext-fonts

Keep the CTFonts that lay out text instead of making new ones per line.
CoreText keeps a font's shaping tables, ASCII advances and fallback faces on
the CTFont object, so a fresh copy per line set them all up again.

- Each font at each size it is laid out in is made once (`sized`).
- The face CoreText falls back to for a CJK character (Han, kana, CJK and
  full-width punctuation) the font has no glyph for is kept, as CoreText made
  it, per font, size and character (`cjk_fallbacks`), and set on that
  character in later lines, so CoreText does not fall back again. Taking
  CoreText's own face keeps weight and variation (a bold heading's fallback
  is bold); `CTFontCreateForString` did not.

Laying out text not seen before (dragging the scrollbar of a long Chinese
document) took about a third of the time. Rendering is unchanged (same
glyphs, positions and faces; docs/PERFORMANCE.md).

